# Upstream snapshot — fetched, never committed (ADR-0004). data/derived/ IS
# committed (ADR-0042, supersedes ADR-0028) — do not add it here.
data/upstream/

# The graph is committed in full — all four files (ADR-0070, supersedes
# ADR-0060). The owner ruled on OQ-0005: "Store everything, so the graph can be
# read without building it." It costs about 6.5MB, and it buys someone reading
# what the graph says without a snapshot fetch and a build first.
#
# Nothing is git-ignored here. `data/upstream/` stays ignored under ADR-0004 and
# that is untouched: the snapshot is another repository's corpus and this is a
# derivation of it, the same distinction `data/derived/` already draws.
#
# The cost of committing a generated file is that it can go stale, so
# `tmk-graph --check` fails when it has, and CI runs it (ADR-0070).

# The dashboard's copies of the generated reports.
#
# `site/data/*.json` IS committed — it is what the site reads, and a diff of it
# is a diff of what the published page now says. These four are different: they
# are byte copies of files already committed under `data/derived/reports/`, put
# beside the site so a block can fetch them. Committing them would put the same
# text in the history twice. `tmk-dashboard --write` recreates them.
site/data/reports/

